hostname r4
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.4/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to r3:eth2
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.34.2/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON R4
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP session
!   configure
!   router bgp 65004
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.4
!      neighbor 10.1.34.1 remote-as 65003
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.34.1 activate
!         network 10.0.0.4/32
!      !
!
! TASK 2 — Verify end-to-end propagation
!   With basic BGP up and no community filtering, r4 should see all loopbacks.
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   Expected: 10.0.0.1/32, 10.0.0.2/32, 10.0.0.3/32, 10.0.0.4/32
!
!   Check AS-path for 10.0.0.1/32:
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.0.0.1/32
!   AS-path should be: 65003 65002 65001
!
! TASK 3 — Verify no-export containment
!   After r1 sets community no-export on 10.0.0.1/32:
!   - r2 accepts it but does NOT forward to r3
!   - r3 does NOT forward to r4
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast on r4 should NOT show 10.0.0.1/32
!
! TASK 4 — Verify communities visible on r4
!   If r1 sets community 65001:100 (without no-export) and nobody strips it,
!   r4 should see the community:
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.0.0.1/32
!   Look for "Community: 65001:100" in the output.
!
!   This is how communities signal intent across multiple AS hops.
! ============================================================
end
